examples.question_text:
An L-shaped prism has the uniform cross-section shown and is $9\text{ cm}$ long. Find its volume.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(8,0)--(8,2)--(3,2)--(3,6)--(0,6)--cycle;
\path (4,0) node[below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\path (8,1) node[right] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.5,6) node[above] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\path (0,3) node[left] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Split the cross-section into two rectangles. The upper rectangle has height $6-2=4\text{ cm}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(8,0)--(8,2)--(3,2)--(3,6)--(0,6)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,2)--(3,2);
\path (4,1) node {$A_1$};
\path (1.5,4) node {$A_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}A_1&=8\times2\\&=16\text{ cm}^2\\A_2&=3\times4\\&=12\text{ cm}^2\\A&=16+12\\&=28\text{ cm}^2\\V&=Ah\\&=28\times9\\&=252\text{ cm}^3\end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
A loading ramp has the uniform cross-section shown and is $4\text{ m}$ wide. The bottom is horizontal and both end heights are perpendicular to it. Find the volume of the ramp.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(7,0)--(7,5)--(0,2)--cycle;
\draw (0,0.35)--(0.35,0.35)--(0.35,0);
\draw (6.65,0)--(6.65,0.35)--(7,0.35);
\path (3.5,0) node[below] {$7\text{ m}$};
\path (0,1) node[left] {$2\text{ m}$};
\path (7,2.5) node[right] {$5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Split the cross-section into a rectangle and a triangle. The triangle has perpendicular height $5-2=3\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(7,0)--(7,5)--(0,2)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,2)--(7,2);
\draw[dashed] (7,2)--(7,5);
\path (7,3.5) node[right] {$3\text{ m}$};
\path (3.5,1) node {$A_1$};
\path (5,2.8) node {$A_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}A_1&=7\times2\\&=14\text{ m}^2\\A_2&=\frac{7\times3}{2}\\&=10.5\text{ m}^2\\A&=14+10.5\\&=24.5\text{ m}^2\\V&=Ah\\&=24.5\times4\\&=98\text{ m}^3\end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
A water trough has the uniform trapezium cross-section shown and is $5\text{ m}$ long. Water enters the empty trough at $200\text{ L}$ per minute. Find its volume in cubic metres, its capacity in litres and the time needed to fill it. Use $1\text{ m}^3=1000\text{ L}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=20mm,y=20mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0.8)--(2,0.8)--(1.6,0)--(0.4,0)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (1,0)--(1,0.8);
\draw (1,0.15)--(1.15,0.15)--(1.15,0);
\path (1,0.8) node[above] {$2\text{ m}$};
\path (1,0) node[below] {$1.2\text{ m}$};
\path (1,0.4) node[right] {$0.8\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A prism has the uniform cross-section shown: a $9\text{ cm}$ by $7\text{ cm}$ rectangle with a $3\text{ cm}$ wide, $2\text{ cm}$ deep rectangular notch removed from the top. The prism is $8\text{ cm}$ long. Find the volume of solid material.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(9,0)--(9,7)--(6,7)--(6,5)--(3,5)--(3,7)--(0,7)--cycle;
\path (4.5,0) node[below] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\path (0,3.5) node[left] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\path (4.5,7) node[above] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\path (6,6) node[right] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A prism has a uniform cross-section consisting of a rectangle on top of a trapezium, as shown. The rectangle is $10\text{ mm}$ wide and $5\text{ mm}$ high. The trapezium has parallel sides $10\text{ mm}$ and $18\text{ mm}$ and perpendicular height $9\text{ mm}$. The prism is $20\text{ mm}$ long. Find its volume.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=3mm,y=3mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(18,0)--(14,9)--(14,14)--(4,14)--(4,9)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (4,9)--(14,9);
\draw[dashed] (9,0)--(9,9);
\draw (9,0.7)--(9.7,0.7)--(9.7,0);
\path (9,14) node[above] {$10\text{ mm}$};
\path (14,11.5) node[right] {$5\text{ mm}$};
\path (9,0) node[below] {$18\text{ mm}$};
\path (9,4.5) node[right] {$9\text{ mm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A pool shell has a level top and is $26\text{ m}$ long and $9\text{ m}$ wide. Its uniform side cross-section is shown. The floor is horizontal at a depth of $3\text{ m}$ for the first $8\text{ m}$, then slopes upwards to a depth of $1.5\text{ m}$ at the other end. Find the volume of earth to excavate for the shell to fit exactly.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2mm,y=8mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,3)--(26,3)--(26,1.5)--(8,0)--(0,0)--cycle;
\path (13,3) node[above] {$26\text{ m}$};
\path (0,1.5) node[left] {$3\text{ m}$};
\path (26,2.25) node[right] {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\path (4,0) node[below] {$8\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Split the side cross-section into a rectangle and a trapezium. The sloping section is $26-8=18\text{ m}$ long.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2mm,y=8mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,3)--(26,3)--(26,1.5)--(8,0)--(0,0)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (8,0)--(8,3);
\path (4,1.5) node {$A_1$};
\path (17,2) node {$A_2$};
\path (17,3) node[above] {$18\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}A_1&=8\times3\\&=24\text{ m}^2\\A_2&=\frac{18(3+1.5)}{2}\\&=40.5\text{ m}^2\\A&=24+40.5\\&=64.5\text{ m}^2\\V&=Ah\\&=64.5\times9\\&=580.5\text{ m}^3\end{align*}$
